{"created":"2013-11-21T00:00:00+00:00","revision_id":103,"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1265214?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1265214?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1265214?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1265214?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1265214?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1265214?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1265214"},"updated":"2024-12-04T06:00:11.156242+00:00","metadata":{"publication_info":[{"year":2018,"page_end":"63","page_start":"1","journal_issue":"1","journal_title":"J.Am.Math.Soc.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214160"},"journal_volume":"31"}],"documents":[{"key":"4fa724138833461ce8e816886dfff76d","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/4fa724138833461ce8e816886dfff76d","source":"AMS","filename":"document","fulltext":true}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":66,"citation_count":74,"core":false,"dois":[{"value":"10.1090/jams/888","source":"AMS"},{"value":"10.1090/jams/888","source":"bibmatch"}],"urls":[{"value":"https://www.ams.org/jams/2018-31-01/S0894-0347-2017-00888-9/S0894-0347-2017-00888-9.pdf"}],"titles":[{"title":"Weak null singularities in general relativity","source":"AMS"},{"title":"Weak null singularities in general relativity","source":"arXiv"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"5ac27477-563a-499a-b5ab-5bb14f95e492","emails":["jluk@stanford.edu"],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1913512"},"full_name":"Luk, Jonathan","signature_block":"LACj","raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Mathematics, Stanford University, Stanford, California 94305-2125"}]}],"curated":false,"license":[{"url":"https://www.ams.org/publications/copyright-and-permissions","imposing":"AMS"},{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","imposing":"arXiv"}],"texkeys":["Luk:2013cqa"],"citeable":true,"imprints":[{"date":"2017-09-27"}],"keywords":[{"value":"Einstein equation: vacuum","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"gravitation: collapse","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"singularity","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"integrability","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"black hole","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"stability","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"<p>We construct a class of spacetimes (without symmetry assumptions) satisfying the vacuum Einstein equations with singular boundaries on two null hypersurfaces intersecting in the future on a 2-sphere. The metric of these spacetimes extends continuously beyond the singularities while the Christoffel symbols fail to be square integrable in a neighborhood of any point on the singular boundaries. The construction shows moreover that the singularities are stable in a suitable sense. These singularities are stronger than the impulsive gravitational spacetimes considered by Luk and Rodnianski, and conjecturally they are present in the interior of generic black holes arising from gravitational collapse.</p>","source":"AMS"},{"value":"We construct a class of spacetimes (without symmetry assumptions) satisfying the vacuum Einstein equations with singular boundaries on two null hypersurfaces intersecting in the future on a 2-sphere. The metric of these spacetimes extends continuously beyond the singularities while the Christoffel symbols fail to be square integrable in a neighborhood of any point on the singular boundaries. The construction shows moreover that the singularities are stable in a suitable sense. These singularities are stronger than the impulsive gravitational spacetimes considered by Luk-Rodnianski and conjecturally they are present in the interior of generic black holes arising from gravitational collapse.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/380078"},"reference":{"dois":["10.1098/rspa.1995.0100"],"misc":["1","publisher","print"],"title":{"title":"Structure of the charged spherical black hole interior"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Bonanno, A."}],"publication_info":{"year":1995,"artid":"553","page_start":"553","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214445"},"journal_volume":"450"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/396709"},"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevLett.75.1256"],"misc":["2","publisher","print"],"title":{"title":"Black hole singularities: a numerical approach"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Brady"},{"full_name":"R., Patrick"}],"publication_info":{"year":1995,"artid":"1256","page_start":"1256","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214495"},"journal_volume":"75"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/450254"},"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevLett.79.4958"],"misc":["3","publisher","print"],"title":{"title":"Structure of the black hole’s Cauchy-horizon singularity"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Burko"},{"full_name":"M., Lior"}],"publication_info":{"year":1997,"artid":"4958","page_start":"4958","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214495"},"journal_volume":"79"}}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1098/rspa.1982.0160"],"misc":["4","publisher","print"],"title":{"title":"On crossing the Cauchy horizon of a Reissner-Nordström black-hole"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Chandrasekhar, S."}],"publication_info":{"year":1982,"artid":"301","page_start":"301","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214445"},"journal_volume":"384"}}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.4171/068"],"misc":["5","EMS Monographs in Mathematics","print","publisher","The formation of black holes in general relativity"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou"},{"full_name":"Demetrios"}],"